      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.009342,
      "bytes": 29302,
      "sha256": "56b7ce33d6f6a68de3bfa0d8a85f39434610f49428fd66910c01a80daf0481fd"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-02-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-02-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "Do you have this in a smaller size?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 1.702721,
      "bytes": 19278,
      "sha256": "ec2eb9bc459a08f5d0d0cc60680677fd1a204020e6183cfabec3d278ccb3f118"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-02-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-02-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could I exchange it if it doesn't fit?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.099637,
      "bytes": 22731,
      "sha256": "f76fbb0ecfb92984701e13160cc900a20a850cf7335d4bf17b26eb013df4e1b1"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-02-research",
      "file": "2026-11-02-research.m4a",
      "text": "This method seems promising, but we need more evidence.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.505034,
      "bytes": 33708,
      "sha256": "fbb0684767a28c67dfda90461efe415af0242fa25bdcbfe4a15d7bfb4b837c93"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-02-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-02-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "What are the main advantages and limitations of this approach?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.016463,
      "bytes": 30258,
      "sha256": "780cf8bf58059f42c24da1caa3b12f584f96d5a0b00976cbb51044baef70c09b"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-02-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-02-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "Has this method been tested on a sample similar to ours?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.086621,
      "bytes": 31595,
      "sha256": "c0caaee1ec90b6d131ddad30ef9900c9147a5fe53a51cb13141b83f50ba71e05"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-everyday",
      "file": "2026-11-03-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "Let me check whether I left my umbrella in the office.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.063492,
      "bytes": 31056,
      "sha256": "8b8dbbc62d78df363e9eec2823bda211e4cabb4e89307f910769ef2810fc13ef"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-03-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "Have you seen a blue water bottle anywhere?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.331293,
      "bytes": 24613,
      "sha256": "8a1ffeed7f446f71dc5613896c12b84fef9875578553ef3af7e2122bcd61d1c6"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-03-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could you let me know if anyone hands it in?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.277324,
      "bytes": 24105,
      "sha256": "e6a077bf8cf8ad0aef2f15a957e6befeb0fe71f4d2f02bcc2d866c0f6947a61f"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-research",
      "file": "2026-11-03-research.m4a",
      "text": "We need to check whether the imaging settings were the same.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.899864,
      "bytes": 29498,
      "sha256": "b9fdaa909342e35c4d2b8d97cad0d94bf3b201be2a757ea6b967a3be8a0acac5"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-03-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "Are we comparing images acquired with the same settings?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.086032,
      "bytes": 31673,
      "sha256": "b7514be405da1adc9107c75c438310c246982d7e4c1f6507d4bfd2501b85c162"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-03-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-03-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could the difference come from how the images were processed?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.86585,
      "bytes": 30012,
      "sha256": "15dfd4a67857ef8efe05f172f919d373dcc9f35357ef0200793397deadfaa50a"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-everyday",
      "file": "2026-11-04-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "Would it be okay if we met half an hour later?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.540952,
      "bytes": 26509,
      "sha256": "221423a0df298e2d22e17393136dfa3a28b60bb97459050e2eef2540195a12e4"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-04-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "Something has come up; could we reschedule our meeting?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.19102,
      "bytes": 30791,
      "sha256": "f0a8ad016d46d9588e28d2e045c2d2715591262878501756b25430c194ca3535"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-04-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "Please let me know if the new time is inconvenient.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.838141,
      "bytes": 29387,
      "sha256": "468eff46993e5393ea5cef708240604a37a121a64f00760dd3e88e7d8e72ef52"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-research",
      "file": "2026-11-04-research.m4a",
      "text": "Would it help to compare these samples side by side?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.889252,
      "bytes": 29602,
      "sha256": "8784e48be691015426faadb6e66e5702217febefdc4ab9458afc3ce561dd92c5"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-04-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "Which measurement would best capture the difference we're interested in?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.397914,
      "bytes": 32958,
      "sha256": "dd0a7ea7c00ac2218659a01a2e482c3be07e339a142c22be5b314b2b0a60070a"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-04-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "Should we look at individual samples as well as the group average?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.562676,
      "bytes": 35473,
      "sha256": "b1caa4841e9df6f0fe8be1bbefe1d27620ff0f905f214f6ad369483d6eba1e56"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-everyday",
      "file": "2026-11-05-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "As far as I know, the last bus leaves at midnight.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.143855,
      "bytes": 30255,
      "sha256": "5d715afa75d9a2fe69c48eda2b72cd32b17baf3e611c86f51b8c392f49ffef12"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-05-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "What time do I need to check out tomorrow?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.238639,
      "bytes": 24081,
      "sha256": "a5188273f853dd2d0ff6704f49e94c87dd7c0374b2c310bbb0af439469952190"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-05-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could I leave my luggage here for a few hours?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.50127,
      "bytes": 26001,
      "sha256": "a1116e5c000b47dd02849729ce7dffc9236baae60bc515fc95e92f12149eb13a"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-research",
      "file": "2026-11-05-research.m4a",
      "text": "As far as I understand, the two methods use different labeling strategies.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 4.769252,
      "bytes": 45223,
      "sha256": "ea21b01ce4ca2a259a71de7acce6c8bfbeb1ef9375437f1e87fdc98aa8b06351"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-05-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "The authors address this question by comparing two conditions.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.469524,
      "bytes": 34857,
      "sha256": "2266fb71e8bef692aec71ed229a9a441ffbe2655397b21e02e060a5e0e0f4272"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-05-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-05-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "One limitation is that the study only looked at one cell type.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.522132,
      "bytes": 34775,
      "sha256": "54a7c8188825db2110d94f418327a5aa90f3dc02ff9651e26776766843e0d247"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-everyday",
      "file": "2026-11-06-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "I haven't decided yet, but I'm leaning towards staying in.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.470249,
      "bytes": 33328,
      "sha256": "855b86e5223f4f183c8e0d8c01448a20c936c6ac5845be961ccbdac546c51cad"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-06-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "I'm not feeling well today, so I might head home early.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.421043,
      "bytes": 32626,
      "sha256": "e7fbe638f3f6f2e08d47d7e5e9108a67a3ac042e303a4a0fb96b1798b3f271c9"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-06-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could we take a short break before we carry on?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.624989,
      "bytes": 27464,
      "sha256": "cceef9b49802050aa32fc473d643aeba99de89d4c559ec63792cb4a6ed3c8a3a"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-research",
      "file": "2026-11-06-research.m4a",
      "text": "I'd like to focus on one question at a time.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.610476,
      "bytes": 27469,
      "sha256": "b9f57faa557d6c0246b84714f01bc7eac7e2227fbc604eb31ff8226bbd246891"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-06-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "Which part should I prioritize before our next meeting?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.318957,
      "bytes": 33260,
      "sha256": "4bdf45168292cc35d67e499235894087a68d4b0d35622255abcc9864b4a4e2d8"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-06-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-06-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "Could you take a look at the draft when you have a moment?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.486304,
      "bytes": 26090,
      "sha256": "25755aa4121c396dada0742bda66ad3dab22821afe8f4db6551629c59add78a0"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-everyday-1",
      "file": "2026-11-07-everyday-1.m4a",
      "text": "I'm doing a PhD in Hong Kong, and I'm still getting used to life here.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 4.630884,
      "bytes": 42824,
      "sha256": "57a1f458db333277ba1a8564cf76b4cdf77103123b9017008340a33c3ff303b2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-everyday-2",
      "file": "2026-11-07-everyday-2.m4a",
      "text": "I enjoy cooking, although I don't always have much time for it.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.746122,
      "bytes": 36668,
      "sha256": "48dd54d7b8d7c4fdce3c18d657bfeee2bd2e09c06be77e7ae84d7b1b02c86906"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-everyday-3",
      "file": "2026-11-07-everyday-3.m4a",
      "text": "How did you get interested in that?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 1.72712,
      "bytes": 19482,
      "sha256": "bb1d2daefecaf33ec8709abe6cc4052199c829062b0ded8393ddfb64e3a36609"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-research-1",
      "file": "2026-11-07-research-1.m4a",
      "text": "My research focuses on using expansion microscopy to study small cellular structures.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 5.581497,
      "bytes": 51097,
      "sha256": "91f82ae0f02d046dac334295141c332909ceb2d7dd2763450d7b4c05e50a3b6b"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-research-2",
      "file": "2026-11-07-research-2.m4a",
      "text": "The main question is how well the method preserves the original structure.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.770476,
      "bytes": 36940,
      "sha256": "5814d9f33a66d275ddcccbc441a00c1d289941848dd0b5584921bd4a51029aec"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-11-07-research-3",
      "file": "2026-11-07-research-3.m4a",
      "text": "I'd be interested to hear how you would approach this problem.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.115465,
      "bytes": 31351,
      "sha256": "418d51a6190c0cb3b19a4e5131881701b610afc1a5507b4cb43ac6dfea976769"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-10-24-research",
      "file": "2026-10-24-research.m4a",
      "text": "Could we go over this result together?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 1.905805,
      "bytes": 21564,
      "sha256": "683dd4905c80bf891a917d5e735e2aea1595e60c2bbe6872d2bdf607e574d6ba"
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-10-24-everyday",
      "file": "2026-10-24-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "Do you have time for a quick coffee?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 1.950295,
      "bytes": 21929,
      "sha256": "9abfb68297ab60009eeaf95debc8fc930ab6e77dcea042d7be687a018dbf86ac"
    },
    {
      "id": "thu-everyday",
      "file": "thu-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "Could you show me how to use this machine?",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.056735,
      "bytes": 22255,
      "sha256": "d5fd3ad802b46bf69d71b61a7a9195a84db8ba8720c7b5cf9b68301de7eeda27"
    },
    {
      "id": "thu-research",
      "file": "thu-research.m4a",
      "text": "The main idea is to expand the sample before imaging it.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.387347,
      "bytes": 33911,
      "sha256": "109af45e44586202c9d1a299addbba238c91d982a56ace55c621cb2a66d82e94"
    },
    {
      "id": "fri-everyday",
      "file": "fri-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "I'd rather go somewhere quiet so we can have a proper chat.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.42195,
      "bytes": 34259,
      "sha256": "6dade49dbaf2bec9e0a8cd1c30604a0d0657e330b7b655f5c251ded4e7629a0d"
    },
    {
      "id": "fri-research",
      "file": "fri-research.m4a",
      "text": "This allows us to see details that are normally too close together.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.734966,
      "bytes": 36469,
      "sha256": "5ff0ab629412d1741a3c57dab06a0c81ef9438416b0dee7e0030eaa2477482b1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hihomo-full",
      "file": "hihomo-full.m4a",
      "text": "This paper asks a simple question: can we make a sample much larger without changing its shape? Expansion microscopy helps us see small structures by physically expanding a sample. However, a large expansion factor alone does not tell us whether the expansion is uniform. The researchers developed a method called high-fold homogeneous expansion microscopy. They reported about eight- to nine-fold expansion in a single round and tested structural preservation in centrioles and nuclear pore complexes. The method also supports labeling after expansion. The main point is to check both how much a sample expands and how well its structure is preserved.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 40.833288,
      "bytes": 341807,
      "sha256": "3685fb0cbfd5a696045b32075450e8959fafbff7975f40b910655d330afc41fb"
    },
    {
      "id": "hihomo-1",
      "file": "hihomo-1.m4a",
      "text": "This paper asks a simple question: can we make a sample much larger without changing its shape? Expansion microscopy helps us see small structures by physically expanding a sample. However, a large expansion factor alone does not tell us whether the expansion is uniform.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 17.160544,
      "bytes": 144557,
      "sha256": "bfc0b44bc22371482395bde2e690b46ab8d36d2b4ebba0033cd9e71416c78435"
    },
    {
      "id": "hihomo-2",
      "file": "hihomo-2.m4a",
      "text": "The researchers developed a method called high-fold homogeneous expansion microscopy. They reported about eight- to nine-fold expansion in a single round and tested structural preservation in centrioles and nuclear pore complexes. The method also supports labeling after expansion. The main point is to check both how much a sample expands and how well its structure is preserved.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 23.473424,
      "bytes": 197619,
      "sha256": "e3fab09177598ee9b3c4eec1e3cc6cd1cf99ee5b1345b37f71916145a489c494"
    },
    {
      "id": "mon-everyday",
      "file": "mon-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "Let me check my schedule and get back to you.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 2.390113,
      "bytes": 25654,
      "sha256": "bb5db0adf79183e37c68c4c824c492d2cefbcc624e5b4f5f81ca1dab35f238fd"
    },
    {
      "id": "mon-research",
      "file": "mon-research.m4a",
      "text": "I'm trying to understand why these samples look so different.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.597596,
      "bytes": 35669,
      "sha256": "830e4f8b1f49e1f63bd87090c58c6418e458a03125f93fc885f904c29733c3d1"
    },
    {
      "id": "tue-everyday",
      "file": "tue-everyday.m4a",
      "text": "It took longer than I expected, so I got back late.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
      "rate": 175,
      "seconds": 3.412063,
      "bytes": 33356,
      "sha256": "4044a04f772e86c34d259c42b38d33af7ca31194beed256403378cfaa200ae75"
    },
    {
      "id": "tue-research",
      "file": "tue-research.m4a",
      "text": "I changed one step, but the result was still the same.",
      "voice": "Ava (Enhanced)",
      "language": "en-US",
